{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>From YHWH</b> — the meaning of 'steps' [מצעדי] is his movements." "<b>A man</b> [גבר] — in our language it means one full of understanding, as in: 'go now, the men' [הגברים]. And whoever is full of understanding will be righteous." "<b>And His way He desires</b> — HaShem desires all his ways. And if he [the wicked] lacks a bet [i.e., lacks understanding], therefore he will not succeed."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {2 "The argument that a missing bet is linked to failure is cryptic; rendered hyper-literally without expansion."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:30:00.402664506Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}